<section class="permission-guide" aria-labelledby="truenas-api-permissions-title">
    <div class="permission-guide-header">
        <div>
            <h3 id="truenas-api-permissions-title">TrueNAS API permissions</h3>
            <p>Grant only the roles needed for the features you use.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/help#api-permissions">Permission help</a>
    </div>

    <div class="permission-grid">
        <article class="permission-card required">
            <span class="permission-label">Required</span>
            <div class="permission-role-list"><code>APPS_READ</code><code>APPS_WRITE</code></div>
            <p>Installed-app inventory, health, logs, lifecycle actions, updates, and rollback.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="permission-card discover">
            <span class="permission-label">Discover gallery</span>
            <div class="permission-role-list"><code>CATALOG_READ</code></div>
            <p>Catalog browsing and app details. This is separate from <code>APPS_READ</code>.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="permission-card optional">
            <span class="permission-label">Optional system panels</span>
            <div class="permission-role-list"><code>POOL_READ</code><code>ALERT_LIST_READ</code><code>SYSTEM_UPDATE_READ</code></div>
            <p><code>READONLY_ADMIN</code> adds broader host details and all read roles; use it only when that wider access is acceptable.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="permission-card optional">
            <span class="permission-label">System performance</span>
            <div class="permission-role-list"><code>REPORTING_READ</code></div>
            <p>Realtime host and pool activity plus historical CPU, memory, load, network, disk I/O, ZFS ARC, and temperatures.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="permission-card optional">
            <span class="permission-label">Data Protection Center</span>
            <div class="permission-role-list"><code>DATASET_READ</code><code>SNAPSHOT_READ</code><code>SNAPSHOT_TASK_READ</code><code>REPLICATION_TASK_READ</code><code>CLOUD_SYNC_READ</code></div>
            <p>Dataset coverage, newest snapshot age, replication and cloud-sync state, schedules, and unprotected warnings.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="permission-card optional">
            <span class="permission-label">Drive &amp; Pool Health</span>
            <div class="permission-role-list"><code>POOL_READ</code><code>DISK_READ</code><code>REPORTING_READ</code><code>ALERT_LIST_READ</code></div>
            <p>Pool topology and scans, disk identity and membership, cached temperature, ZFS errors, and SMART-related alerts.</p>
        </article>
    </div>

    <p class="permission-note"><strong>Changed a privilege?</strong> Run <strong>Test connection</strong> or use <strong>Reconnect &amp; retry</strong> on Discover so the new TrueNAS session receives it.</p>
</section>
